Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-06-11
Subject: Compare real defaults by Pascal payload bytes
License: expat

FPC 3.2.0 compares real default parameter constants bytewise when matching a
forward declaration with its implementation.  That is intentional: it lets the
same NaN default match itself while still treating distinct real encodings,
such as +0.0 and -0.0, as different declarations.

The comparison must only cover the defined Pascal real payload.  In the Linux
bootstrap target matrix, the FPC 3.2.0 compiler sources define bestreal as
Extended for i386 and x86_64, and as Double for arm, aarch64, powerpc and
powerpc64.  The x86 Extended payload is 10 bytes, but the translated compiler
may store it in a C++ long double object whose ABI storage is wider.  Those
extra bytes are translated-storage padding, not Pascal value bytes, so
comparing them makes identical real defaults depend on unspecified padding
contents.

Limit wider-than-double translated storage to the 10-byte Pascal x87 payload.
Targets whose bestreal is double keep the existing full-size comparison.

--- a/compiler/symutil.pas
+++ b/compiler/symutil.pas
@@ -56,6 +56,23 @@ implementation
     function equal_constsym(sym1,sym2:tconstsym; nanequal: boolean):boolean;
       var
         p1,p2,pend : pchar;
+
+      function real_const_compare_size: longint;
+        begin
+          result:=sizeof(pbestreal^);
+          { Real default values are compared bytewise when nanequal is set so
+            that NaN defaults match the same NaN bit pattern, and so distinct
+            real encodings such as +0.0 and -0.0 remain distinct during
+            forward/implementation header matching.  That bytewise comparison
+            must cover only the Pascal real payload.  x87 Extended carries a
+            10-byte payload, while translated C++ long double storage can be
+            wider because of ABI padding.  In the Linux bootstrap matrix this
+            affects i386 and x86_64; arm, aarch64, powerpc and powerpc64 have
+            bestreal=double and keep the full double-sized value. }
+          if result>sizeof(double) then
+            result:=10;
+        end;
+
       begin
         equal_constsym:=false;
         if sym1.consttyp<>sym2.consttyp then
@@ -91,7 +108,7 @@ implementation
              end;
            constreal :
              if nanequal then
-               equal_constsym:=CompareByte(pbestreal(sym1.value.valueptr)^,pbestreal(sym2.value.valueptr)^,sizeof(pbestreal^))=0
+               equal_constsym:=CompareByte(pbestreal(sym1.value.valueptr)^,pbestreal(sym2.value.valueptr)^,real_const_compare_size)=0
              else
                equal_constsym:=pbestreal(sym1.value.valueptr)^=pbestreal(sym2.value.valueptr)^;
            constset :
